<title>Libya: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/libya/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-libya-2026-11-27T05:12:49.123Z</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:12:49 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Ukrainian naval drones have struck two Russian vessels at Libya's Benghazi port and off its coast, sinking one warship and damaging another, which Ukraine described as self-defence. Libyan forces say two of their naval officers were killed in the Ukrainian attack on the Russian warship. The attacks have prompted threats of retaliation from Libyan militias and promises of reprisal from the Libyan army. The conflict still records only two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/25/world/middleeast/libya-ukraine-russia-haftar.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
